# Linux 7.2.12 camera stack for the lmi (Xiaomi POCO F2 Pro) experiment.
#
# Scope: this fragment adds ONLY the camera path of the lmi board. Everything
# else stays exactly as validated by configs/observer-tested.config, which is
# the config that produced the accepted observer boot.
#
# Why this fragment exists: the observer config carries no media stack at all,
# so the kernel has no V4L2 core, no media controller, no CSI-2 receiver, no
# ISP and no sensor. On the permanent Linux 7.2.12 boot of the handset the
# camera stack is present and probed: the camss platform device ac6a000.camss
# registers and exposes fourteen msm_vfe*_video nodes, while the rear sensor
# node does not bind. The symbols below are exactly the ones the running
# handset configuration carries for that path, read from its own
# /proc/config.gz, so the fragment reproduces a configuration that is already
# proven on the device instead of a guessed one.
#
# THE CHAIN HAS TO BE ENABLED AS A WHOLE. The camera path is not a single
# symbol: the sensor driver sits behind the camera sub-menu of the media
# support, and the CAMSS driver additionally requires the V4L2 platform
# driver layer, which itself requires VIDEO_DEV and the media controller. A
# fragment that only sets the two driver symbols is silently dropped by
# olddefconfig, because the symbols that make them reachable are missing.
# That is the reason this fragment lists the whole chain.
#
# CONFIG_MEDIA_SUPPORT, CONFIG_MEDIA_CAMERA_SUPPORT, CONFIG_MEDIA_PLATFORM_SUPPORT:
# the media support and its camera and platform sub-menus. The rear sensor
# driver of this board is an Omnivision OV13B10 (48 MP main sensor), described
# in the board device tree as compatible "ovti,ov13b10".
# CONFIG_VIDEO_OV13B10: that sensor driver. It is built in on the handset and
# registers, so the missing piece is not the driver but its matching, which is
# what patches/0004-lmi-ov13b10-of-match.patch restores.
# CONFIG_MEDIA_CONTROLLER: the media controller API, used by the sensor and by
# the CAMSS driver to bind the sensor to the CSI-2 receiver through the device
# tree graph.
# CONFIG_VIDEO_DEV, CONFIG_V4L_PLATFORM_DRIVERS, CONFIG_V4L2_ASYNC,
# CONFIG_V4L2_FWNODE, CONFIG_VIDEO_V4L2_SUBDEV_API, CONFIG_VIDEOBUF2_DMA_SG,
# CONFIG_VIDEO_CAMERA_SENSOR: the V4L2 core and the subdev, asynchronous
# notifier, fwnode graph and buffer allocator that the sensor subdev and the
# CAMSS driver need.
# CONFIG_VIDEO_QCOM_CAMSS: the camera subsystem of this board is the mainline
# CAMSS driver with its SM8250 resource set, matched through the compatible
# "qcom,sm8250-camss". It brings the CSI-2 receiver, the CSID and the VFE
# ISP, and it is what creates the fourteen video nodes of the handset.
#
# BUILT-IN, NOT MODULE: the observer initramfs carries no module payload, so
# every symbol on this path has to be compiled in. With CONFIG_VIDEO_OV13B10=m
# the driver would never load from that initramfs and the sensor would never
# bind, with no message to explain it.
CONFIG_MEDIA_SUPPORT=y
CONFIG_MEDIA_CAMERA_SUPPORT=y
CONFIG_MEDIA_PLATFORM_SUPPORT=y
CONFIG_MEDIA_CONTROLLER=y
CONFIG_VIDEO_DEV=y
CONFIG_V4L_PLATFORM_DRIVERS=y
CONFIG_V4L2_ASYNC=y
CONFIG_V4L2_FWNODE=y
CONFIG_VIDEO_V4L2_SUBDEV_API=y
CONFIG_VIDEOBUF2_DMA_SG=y
CONFIG_VIDEO_CAMERA_SENSOR=y
CONFIG_VIDEO_OV13B10=y
CONFIG_VIDEO_QCOM_CAMSS=y
